.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt SMIME_READ_CMS 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm SMIME_read_CMS_ex ,
.Nm SMIME_read_CMS
.Nd parse S/MIME message
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/cms.h
.Ft CMS_ContentInfo *
.Fo SMIME_read_CMS_ex
.Fa "BIO *bio"
.Fa "int flags"
.Fa "BIO **bcont"
.Fa "CMS_ContentInfo **cms"
.Fc
.Ft CMS_ContentInfo *
.Fo SMIME_read_CMS
.Fa "BIO *in"
.Fa "BIO **bcont"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn SMIME_read_CMS
parses a message in S/MIME format.
.Pp
.Fa in
is a BIO to read the message from.
.Pp
If cleartext signing is used then the content is saved in a memory bio
which is written to
.Sy *bcont ,
otherwise
.Sy *bcont
is set to NULL.
.Pp
The parsed CMS_ContentInfo structure is returned or NULL if an error
occurred.
.Pp
.Fn SMIME_read_CMS_ex
is similar to
.Fn SMIME_read_CMS
but optionally a previously created
.Fa cms
CMS_ContentInfo object can be supplied as well as some
.Fa flags .
To create a
.Fa cms
object use
.Xr CMS_ContentInfo_new_ex 3 .
If the
.Fa flags
argument contains
.Sy CMS_BINARY
then the input is assumed to be in binary format and is not translated
to canonical form.
If in addition
.Sy SMIME_ASCIICRLF
is set then the binary input is assumed to be followed by
.Sy CR
and
.Sy LF
characters, else only by an
.Sy LF
character.
If
.Fa flags
is 0 and
.Fa cms
is NULL then it is identical to
.Fn SMIME_read_CMS .
.Sh NOTES
If
.Sy *bcont
is not NULL then the message is clear text signed.
.Sy *bcont
can then be passed to
.Xr CMS_verify 3
with the
.Sy CMS_DETACHED
flag set.
.Pp
Otherwise the type of the returned structure can be determined using
.Xr CMS_get0_type 3 .
.Pp
To support future functionality if
.Fa bcont
is not NULL
.Sy *bcont
should be initialized to NULL. For example:
.Bd -literal
 BIO *cont = NULL;
 CMS_ContentInfo *cms;

 cms = SMIME_read_CMS(in, &cont);
.Ed
.Sh BUGS
The MIME parser used by
.Fn SMIME_read_CMS
is somewhat primitive.
While it will handle most S/MIME messages more complex compound formats
may not work.
.Pp
The parser assumes that the CMS_ContentInfo structure is always base64
encoded and will not handle the case where it is in binary format or
uses quoted printable format.
.Pp
The use of a memory BIO to hold the signed content limits the size of
message which can be processed due to memory restraints: a streaming
single pass option should be available.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn SMIME_read_CMS_ex
and
.Fn SMIME_read_CMS
return a valid
.Vt CMS_ContentInfo
structure or
.Dv NULL
if an error occurred.
The error can be obtained from ERR_get_error(3).
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ERR_get_error 3 ,
.Xr CMS_sign 3 ,
.Xr CMS_verify 3 ,
.Xr CMS_encrypt 3 ,
.Xr CMS_decrypt 3
.Sh HISTORY
The function
.Fn SMIME_read_CMS_ex
was added in OpenSSL 3.0.
